{#- The shell for the pages a mail's turn-off link opens
    (services/web-api routes/email.mjs). The API reads this built
    document from the site bucket, writes its own title and replaces the
    section marked data-email-page with the step the link is at: confirm,
    turned off, an expired link, an email that has ended. Its words live
    there; what is here is only what the address shows if someone opens
    it directly. Every class the API writes is used below, so the
    stylesheet keeps it. Served at /api/email/unsubscribe, so every link
    is absolute. Never in the sitemap and never indexed. -#}
<section class="mx-auto flex max-w-[560px] flex-col items-start gap-4 pt-10 pb-6" data-email-page>
  <span class="chip">Email</span>
  <h1 class="hero-title m-0">Your Elixir email</h1>
  <p class="docs__lede m-0">
    Every email Elixir sends has a switch of its own. Choose which ones you
    get from your email settings, and turn any of them back on there.
  </p>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3" data-session-face="out">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signin">Sign in</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/">Elixir home</a>
    <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/docs/email">How Elixir email works</a>
  </div>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3" data-session-face="in">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/settings/emails">Email settings</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/home">Open Home</a>
    <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/docs/email">How Elixir email works</a>
  </div>
</section>
